      "body": "Current exact-head CI 38252891691 attempt1 completed with failure. Standard installation/reentry and the untraced fresh repair/move/uninstall journey passed; traced repair.apply exceeded its unchanged public deadline. Recovery, initial refusal, bootstrap and SDK consumer checks were skipped. Six other jobs passed. This draft remains unqualified and is not integrated into dev or main.\n\nOriginal traced client 2548 was live with no native response or stdout/stderr at its deadline. The independent observer failed during read_current_native_objects with an unavailable metadata handle and no row set; its token-handle-closure flag is false. Current journal, effect and custody states are unavailable. Predecessor b63 completed/sealed diagnostic metadata does not establish this request's state, completion, restoration, cause or cure. Both current original fresh probe archives and exact failure facts are retained.\n\nCurrent head 0fc1f90de0699379a0b4064b805d86fc51a7332f; tree 71cad4fb2c415ab1d5db87c6c9a66a37d1313ff4.\n\nRepeated Windows file hashes now reuse the immutable explicit Microsoft SHA-256 provider owned by their exact held StableFile. Each call still creates and destroys a separate hash and rereads every byte in the existing 64 KiB chunks. Lazy synchronized initialization leaves non-hash construction and reads independent of CNG. Native observations, full endpoint validation, ordered access queries, byte/identity/path/time checks, fences, effect ordering and deadlines remain intact. No digest, file-observation or authority cache, global resource, provider fallback or pseudo-handle is added.\n\nLocal validation passed independent source review/full root acknowledgment, the coherent Release rebuild and 16 native controls, 435 Python controls and required policy checks. Concurrent hashes and interleaved offset reads use independent portable SHA/source-byte oracles; existing boundary, fresh-content and refusal checks remain. Private Windows C++ layout changes require affected consumers to rebuild; C ABI1.0, encodings and platform floor are unchanged. Provider lifetime and allocation/provider-open failure chronology change. Exact-head hosted qualification failed; no benefit or cure is claimed.\n\nPredecessor b63eb94 CI38240571262 attempt1 passed standard installation/reentry and untraced fresh repair/move/uninstall. Traced repair.apply exceeded its unchanged deadline; its original client was live with no native response and unknown outcome. Later completed transaction/sealed-effect metadata does not complete that client. Recovery, initial refusal, bootstrap and SDK consumer checks were skipped. Original trace/image/symbol joins and bounded late CPU exports are retained; overlapping samples identify file hashing and authority/original-record processing as source leads, without proving whole cost or deadline cause.\n\nAIDE main 6f2abc4 is included with project customizations preserved. Inventory remains 29 implemented, 65 partial, 46 absent and 4 unverified; all 144 acceptance statuses remain not_run. Foundation 1.1, the wider specification and ordinary public SDK strict installation remain unfinished. Draft until seven exact-head jobs, the finite 24 publisher obligations, separate initial refusal, genuinely ended source-free recovery/retries, four actual SDK consumer modes, dataset review and final head/base/live-policy checks pass. Standing authorization covers qualified normal dev integration and main promotion.\n",
